# Line endings for GENERATED, TRACKED files - the ones a script rewrites in place.
#
# THE PHANTOM THIS KILLS. Windows checkouts here run with `core.autocrlf=true`, so git writes these
# files to the working tree with CRLF and caches that size in the index. Every generator below
# writes plain "\n". After `npm run build` the bytes are therefore SHORTER than the index expects,
# and git reports the file as modified - while `git diff` shows nothing at all, because the cleaned
# content hashes to the very same blob. Nothing changed; the file just looks changed.
#
# WHAT IT COST. `scripts/merge-order.mjs` and `scripts/safe-merge-preflight.mjs` both refuse to act
# on a dirty worktree, correctly. On 2026-08-21 that phantom marked TWO branches NOT LANDABLE
# (claude/migration-0040-1f501a, claude/template-width-scaling-5dd0a6) over zero changed lines, and
# blocked a safe-merge run mid-flight. A session that runs the build looks unlandable to every tool
# that asks "is this tree clean?".
#
# `text eol=lf` makes checkout write LF, which is what the generators write and what git already
# stores - so the working tree, the index and the generator finally agree. Add a path here when a
# script starts rewriting a tracked file in place; nothing else belongs in this file.

# Rewritten by scripts/build-production-pack.mjs on EVERY `npm run build`.
public/packs/*.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by the catalog sweeps and by `npm run record:e2e-durations`.
e2e/catalog-baseline.json text eol=lf
e2e/catalog-render-baseline.json text eol=lf
scripts/e2e-durations.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by cli/scripts/build-skill.mjs (every `npm --prefix cli run build`; `--check` in the
# root build): the plugin's skill copy, the version-stamped manifests, the package LICENSE.
cli/plugin/skills/** text eol=lf
cli/plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json text eol=lf
cli/plugin/.codex-plugin/plugin.json text eol=lf
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json text eol=lf
cli/LICENSE text eol=lf
